"""Consolidate duplicate explanations without changing formulas or results."""
from pathlib import Path
def change(s,a,b):
    assert s.count(a)==1,(a[:90],s.count(a))
    return s.replace(a,b)
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'manuscript/main.tex'
s=p.read_text()
s=change(s,'How Many Scores Certify Retention of Language Outputs under a Churn Budget?','How Many Scores Certify Output Retention under a Churn Budget?')
s=change(s,'A curator may retain some selections and refer other decisions for review. The trade-off concerns retained count and replacement sensitivity; agreement alone does not establish quality','A curator may retain some selections and defer others for review, trading retained count against replacement sensitivity. Agreement alone does not establish quality')
s=change(s,'Here, review means deferring a baseline decision; subsequent human decisions and review costs are not modeled.','Review denotes deferral, without a model of subsequent human decisions or costs.')
s=change(s,'One commitment mask, identifying accepted baseline decisions, is assessed across that family. Retention has no fixed-size or per-prompt quota. The churn budget is an average over replacements, not a bound for each replacement.','A commitment mask identifies accepted baseline decisions across that family. Retention has no fixed-size or per-prompt quota; the budget averages over replacements.')
s=change(s,'Expected risk control need not certify the current batch, while full-matrix evaluation does not identify the least evidence needed. Sufficient evidence and its discovery are two parts of our question.','Expected risk control need not certify the current batch; full-matrix evaluation need not identify minimum evidence. We distinguish sufficient evidence from its discovery.')
s=change(s,'For mean and median pooling, partial scores give safe and optimistic retained counts whose gap certifies shortfall from the full-information optimum.','Partial scores give safe and optimistic retained counts whose gap certifies shortfall from the full-information optimum.')
s=change(s,'NLP replays compare discovery with matching minima. Joint evidence improves on separate proofs in predefined small mean-pooling batches; full-batch interventions show that true row totals need not reduce discovery cost. Controlled panels vary column sharing at fixed row costs. Protocol controls change the task and remain separate from same-task order comparisons.','NLP replays compare discovery with matching minima. Joint evidence improves on separate proofs in small mean-pooling batches; full-batch interventions show that true row totals need not reduce queries. Controlled panels vary column sharing; protocol controls change the task.')
s=change(s,'Our median model assigns unit value to each output and counts oppositions as cost. Sorted prefixes give the full-information optimum; entries or shared columns certify it.','Our median model has unit output value and opposition-count cost. Sorting gives the full-information optimum; entries or shared columns certify it.')
s=change(s,'An even-sized median averages the two central scores; the closed-form median witnesses below require odd $M$. Cutoff ties are included.','Even-sized medians average the two central scores; the median witness formulas require odd $M$. Cutoff ties are included.')
s=change(s,'An acceptable replacement-average allowance of $\\rho$ membership changes sets $\\alpha=\\rho/(2k)$; for $k=10$, an allowance of two flips gives $\\alpha=.10$. It gives no per-replacement bound.','An average allowance of $\\rho$ membership changes sets $\\alpha=\\rho/(2k)$; two flips with $k=10$ give $\\alpha=.10$. This gives no per-replacement bound.')
s=change(s,'Baseline exclusions add no returned outputs, so no dedicated entry queries certify them; whole-column queries still reveal all $N$ rows.','Exclusions add no returned outputs and receive no dedicated entry queries; columns still reveal all $N$ rows.')
s=change(s,'Upper-cost feasibility implies true feasibility. Every true-feasible mask is lower-cost feasible. Maximizing cardinality gives the stated count bounds.','Upper-cost feasibility implies true feasibility, which implies lower-cost feasibility. Maximizing cardinality gives the count bounds.')
s=change(s,'Among active rows with at least one unqueried candidate score, reference priority selects the smallest estimated total flip cost: observed flips plus predictions for remaining entries.','Among query-eligible rows, reference priority selects the smallest estimated total cost: observed flips plus predictions for remaining entries.')
s=change(s,'The first seven evaluators in the fixed Appendix~\\ref{app:protocol} order form the base pool; the others are candidates: $T=7$ for RewardBench and $T=17$ for both WMT23 panels.','The first seven evaluators in Appendix~\\ref{app:protocol} form the base pool; the remaining $T=7$ RewardBench or $T=17$ WMT23 evaluators are candidates.')
s=change(s,'The primary stop uses integer gap $\\varepsilon=\\lceil.02|S_0(P)|\\rceil$: the nominal 2\\% fraction is rounded up to whole outputs. Exact stopping uses zero gap.','Primary stopping uses integer gap $\\varepsilon=\\lceil.02|S_0(P)|\\rceil$, rounding the nominal 2\\% fraction up to whole outputs; exact stopping uses zero gap.')
s=change(s,'At $\\alpha=.10$, we record checkpoints at 0, 10, 25, 50 and 100\\% of active entries. If exact certification precedes a later inspection checkpoint, its state is reused without further queries.','At $\\alpha=.10$, checkpoints cover 0, 10, 25, 50 and 100\\% of active entries, reusing the exact-stop state for later checkpoints.')
s=change(s,'Reference and base-pool scoring are counted separately. Counts start after panel construction and exclude full-panel WMT23 preprocessing reads, including later test outputs. They do not measure acquisition savings from initial data collection.','Reference and base scoring are counted separately. Acquisition counts exclude panel construction and full-panel WMT23 preprocessing reads, including later test outputs; they do not measure initial-collection savings.')
s=change(s,'Under median pooling, mean paired reference-minus-comparator precision differences are','With median pooling, mean paired precision differences (reference minus comparator) are')
s=change(s,'Under reference priority on RewardBench at $q=.05$, $\\alpha=.10$ and the primary positive-gap stop, median-pooling entry queries reveal','On RewardBench, reference priority at $q=.05$, $\\alpha=.10$ and the primary stop reveals')
# The next sentence explicitly assigns both pairs to their pooling rule.
s=change(s,'of all $NT$ candidate-test scores versus 71.8\\% through columns; under mean pooling, the fractions','of $NT$ candidate-test scores versus 71.8\\% through columns under median pooling; under mean pooling, the fractions')
s=change(s,'the corresponding minimum exact median column certificate on thirteen-stream WMT23 reveals','the corresponding thirteen-stream WMT23 minimum reveals')
s=change(s,'The required score evidence depends on how observations support feasibility and exclusion under the fixed churn task. Median agreements and oppositions give separate minima; the joint row-state program counts evidence serving both proofs, including existing observations. Initial bounds determine whether acquisition is needed, and matching minima separate evidence requirements from discovery cost. Full-batch interventions show that accurate row totals alone do not ensure efficient discovery. Protocol changes and column sharing alter the task or available evidence. These certificates establish retention guarantees; quality and execution savings require separate evidence.','Score evidence must establish feasibility and exclude larger retained sets under the fixed churn task. Median evidence separates; the joint row-state program counts observations serving both proofs, including existing evidence. Initial bounds determine whether querying is needed; matching minima distinguish requirements from discovery. Full-batch interventions show that accurate row totals need not improve discovery. Protocol changes and column sharing alter the task or available evidence. Quality and execution savings require separate evidence.')
p.write_text(s)
